class.description:
A [FlowGraphValidation] lists the problems that [method FlowGraph.validate] found. Each issue has a kind ([enum IssueKind]), the id of the node it is about and a message. Issues that are not about one node, such as a missing start node, use [constant FlowGraph.NODE_ID_NONE] as node id. The object is a snapshot and does not change when the graph changes.
[method is_valid] is [code]true[/code] if there are no issues at all. Warnings of nodes ([constant ISSUE_KIND_NODE_WARNING]) count as issues too.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var validation := graph.validate()
if not validation.is_valid():
	for i in validation.get_issue_count():
		print(validation.get_issue_node_id(i), ": ", validation.get_issue_message(i))
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
FlowGraphValidation validation = graph.Validate();
if (!validation.IsValid())
{
    for (int i = 0; i < validation.GetIssueCount(); i++)
    {
        GD.Print(validation.GetIssueNodeId(i), ": ", validation.GetIssueMessage(i));
    }
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
